<title>DENMARK: ISS acquires 49 pct of Swedish firm.</title>
<headline>ISS acquires 49 pct of Swedish firm.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish cleaning group International Service System (ISS) said on Monday it acquired a 49 percent shareholding in Swedish home-help domestic services firm Hemfrid AB for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>It said Hemrid was a company which carried out cleaning and household functions including collecting children from kindergarten.</p>
<p>The share takeover was carried out by ISS' Swedish subsidiary ISS Scandinavia, ISS said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
